 "final_result": "Built a three-script Python workflow for zincblende CdTe (Materials Project ID: mp-406, space group F-43m #216).\n\n**Workflow outline:**\n1. **STEP 1 (reduce_cell.py):** Fetched CdTe from Materials Project (mp-406, F-43m #216). Original cell had 2 atoms (Cd, Te); primitive cell from kp_atoms(standard_kpath(atoms)) also has 2 atoms, same space group F-43m (#216). Written to structures/structure_000.cif.\n\n2. **STEP 2 (generate_structures.py):** Generated 51 structures (000-050). Structure 000 is unperturbed; 001-050 have random thermal displacements (Einstein model at 300 K, Cd RMS=0.1314 A, Te RMS=0.1128 A) plus small random lattice strain (max 0.5%). CdTe is stable at room temperature (melting point ~1045 K), so 300 K is representative. Cd (112.4 amu) is lighter than Te (127.6 amu), so Cd has larger displacement.\n\n3. **STEP 3:** Fetched pseudopotentials for Cd and Te (norm-conserving, pbesol, stringent, UPF, scalar-relativistic since Z<54). Cd z_valence=20, Te z_valence=24. Total electrons=44, occupied bands=22, nbnd=44. Cutoffs: Cd 60 Ha=120 Ry, Te 51 Ha=102 Ry, used max=120 Ry for ecutwfc, ecutrho=480 Ry.\n\n4. **STEP 4-5 (setup_jobs.py):** For each structure, created calculations/NNN/ with pseudopotentials, kpath.json, pw.in (SCF), bands.in (NSCF bands), and bands_post.in (bands.x). SCF k-mesh: 7x7x7 (computed via scf_kmesh). Bands k-path: GAMMA-X-U | K-GAMMA-L-W-X (166 k-points). All inputs written with write_espresso_in and validated with validate_qe_input.\n\n5. **STEP 6:** Ran run_espresso_workflow on calculations/000 only. All three steps completed successfully (scf, bands_scf, bands_post).\n\n6. **STEP 7 (plot_bands.py):** Plotted band structure aligned to VBM. VBM=7.567 eV, CBM=8.116 eV, band gap=0.549 eV. Saved to calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.\n\n**ASE functions used:** ase.io.read, ase.io.write, ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in, chem_llm.kpath (standard_kpath, kp_atoms, kp_kpts, kp_save, scf_kmesh, plot_axis), chem_llm.qe_output (read_pw_out, band_edges), chem_llm.tools.upf (read_upf_header).\n\n**Band gap obtained:** 0.549 eV (PBEsol, scalar-relativistic, no spin-orbit).\n\n**Scientific assumptions:**\n- 300 K for thermal displacements (CdTe stable at room temperature)\n- Einstein model with Debye temperatures Cd=150 K, Te=164 K\n- Scalar-relativistic pseudopotentials (Z<54 for both Cd and Te)\n- No spin-orbit coupling (not required for Z<54)\n- occupations='fixed' (CdTe is a semiconductor, gap ~0.59 eV)\n- nspin=1 (non-magnetic, moment 0.0)\n\n**Needs expert review:**\n- The band gap of 0.549 eV is close to the Materials Project value of 0.5867 eV, but PBEsol typically underestimates gaps. A hybrid functional or GW calculation would be needed for quantitative accuracy.\n- The Einstein model for thermal displacements is a simplification; a full phonon calculation would be more accurate.\n- The k-mesh of 7x7x7 was chosen by scf_kmesh; convergence testing would be needed for production calculations.",
